      "message": "Is this issue exclusive to WeChat, or do other VoIP apps exhibit similar behavior? The core question seems to be whether a mid-call change to the remote number should force a termination and restart. Since WeChat handles calls differently than standard PSTN, the root cause might be the AG (Audio Gateway) incorrectly reusing an active call session for a new endpoint. If this CL introduces a logic change to address that, we should flag it so we can assist with the implementation.",
